-- title:
--   Level automorphisms at q=3 descend to the fixed field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field is contained in the one generated by the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(q^2M')$, $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' = \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi$. Let $H_1 = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' \sqcap \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\big)$, let $K = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1)$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$, let $G \le \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K)$ be generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$, and let $K_0 = K^G$. Here $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi'\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma\,K\,\tau$ asserts: for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$'s series nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi' = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota_*\big(\tau x\big)\cdot q\text{-exp}\big(g\mid_k \gamma^{(q)}\big) = q\text{-exp}\big(f\mid_k \gamma^{(q)}\big)$, where $\gamma^{(q)}$ is the conjugate $\mathrm{diag}(1,q)\,\gamma\,\mathrm{diag}(1,q)^{-1}$. Regard $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$. The conclusion: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ consisting exactly of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in the image of $k_0$, and every $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi : K_0 \to F_0$ which is coefficientwise compatible, i.e. the image of the Laurent series of $f \in K_0$ under $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the Laurent series of $\varphi f$, the following holds: for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi' \in k_0$ whose image is $\zeta$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K)$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi'\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma\,K\,\tau$, the automorphism $\tau$ maps $K_0$ into itself, and for all $f \in K_0$ one has $\varphi(\tau f) = (\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma)(\varphi f)$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, where $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ is a chosen automorphism of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying the corresponding $q$-expansion identity at $\zeta$ and $\gamma$ (and the identity if none exists).
--
--   This transports the level automorphisms of the auxiliary field $K$ of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, rigidified by the guard prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, to the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ across the coefficientwise identification $\varphi$ of the fixed field $K^G$ with $F_0$; it is the $q=3$ case of the comparison used to realise the diamond action on the full-level modular function field. It feeds the construction of the algebra isomorphism in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_linkedScalars_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_linkedScalars_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
